# Shell scripts must reach a container with Unix line endings.
#
# Several of the scripts in this repository are executed inside Linux images —
# `deploy/postgres-init/10-roles.sh` by Postgres's entrypoint,
# `deploy/proxy/40-real-ip.sh` by nginx's, `deploy/stack-smoke.sh` by CI. A
# CRLF checkout on Windows turns the shebang into `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` and
# every line into a command with a stray carriage return, which fails as
# `'\r': command not found` — a message that names nothing an operator can act
# on. Normalising here means the file is the same bytes wherever it is checked
# out, which is what a deployment artifact has to be.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same argument, different consumer: these are read by Docker, nginx and
# Compose inside Linux images.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf

# The generated API description, compared **byte for byte** by
# `nx run @plantops/iam-api:openapi:check`.
#
# The emitter writes LF. Without this line, git hands a Windows checkout CRLF,
# so the check reports the document as stale on every run — on a machine where
# nothing is stale — and the fix it suggests (regenerate and commit) produces a
# commit with no content in it. Pinning the checkout to LF makes the check mean
# what it says wherever it runs.
apps/iam-api/openapi.json text eol=lf
